WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience applauds)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.811
- It's nice to see you in person.

00:00:01.811 --> 00:00:02.790
(Alison laughs)
You've been on the show,

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:04.232
I feel like twice, and it's always on Zoom

00:00:04.232 --> 00:00:05.490
'cause of COVID.
- It was on Zoom,

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:06.540
so there was always a delay.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:08.040
I was, you know, it's
just a little tricky.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:08.940
- [Kelly] It feels outta pocket,

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:09.773
no, but I'm so excited to have you here.

00:00:09.773 --> 00:00:11.200
- Yeah, thank you for having me.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.620
- Yes, well it's the holiday season,

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.630
but you're planning a
different one right now, right?

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:17.580
- Oh my gosh, I have been planning

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:18.760
my husband's retirement party.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:19.861
- [Kelly] Oh, that's exciting.

00:00:19.861 --> 00:00:22.440
- And he's a California Highway Patrolman,

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.800
and so it is a big deal to retire, right?

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.720
Like all, every officer
he ever worked with,

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.550
who are now, you know, he trained them,

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.950
but now they're captains and lieutenants.

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:33.750
And so we're pulling
people outta the woodwork

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.550
to come and be a part of this event.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.629
But there's lots of surprises
we've planned for him,

00:00:37.629 --> 00:00:38.700
and you know,

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:39.601
a lot of tradition.
- Is he excited about it?

00:00:39.601 --> 00:00:41.910
- He is, oh my gosh, he's so excited, yes.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:44.372
- Yeah, so you're one of the
reigning queens of Hallmark.

00:00:44.372 --> 00:00:45.205
- Oh.

00:00:45.205 --> 00:00:46.038
(audience claps)
- Everybody-

00:00:46.038 --> 00:00:47.400
- You know, the last time I was here,

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.140
you told us we were like "The Avengers."

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.141
So I'm down-

00:00:50.141 --> 00:00:50.974
- It's "The Avengers" of Hallmark.

00:00:50.974 --> 00:00:51.807
- I'm down for "The Avengers," yeah.

00:00:51.807 --> 00:00:53.190
- "The Avengers" of Hallmark, you three,

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.121
you're in all the movies.

00:00:54.121 --> 00:00:54.954
(Alison laughs)

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:56.040
I've always seen them,
'cause my sister, my mom,

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:56.873
our whole family, everybody loves them.

00:00:56.873 --> 00:00:58.980
- Aww, you're nice.
- So, tell us

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:00.240
about your latest, what's this one?

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:03.210
- Okay, so "Magical
Christmas Village" is so fun

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:04.970
because first of all, it starts with like,

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:08.700
the story of, Marlo Thomas
plays my mom in this movie,

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:09.533
which is amazing.

00:01:09.533 --> 00:01:10.772
I know, amazing.

00:01:10.772 --> 00:01:13.929
But you know, so there's
the real family dynamic

00:01:13.929 --> 00:01:15.982
of her and I having to live together

00:01:15.982 --> 00:01:17.400
right before the holidays.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.890
So it's already like a
stressful time of year.

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:19.723
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:19.723 --> 00:01:20.580
- But she's coming to live with me,

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.450
and we are not people

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.468
who are meant to be living together.

00:01:23.468 --> 00:01:24.301
So-

00:01:24.301 --> 00:01:25.140
- It makes a great comedy.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.146
- I know, it's so great.

00:01:26.146 --> 00:01:29.820
And she's the queen of
comedy, so that was amazing.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.460
And so that part's really like realistic.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:35.550
And then, she brings with her
this family Christmas village.

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:37.440
Have you ever seen those
like amazing villages

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:38.670
that people put in their homes?

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:39.617
Do you have one?

00:01:39.617 --> 00:01:40.450
(audience laughs)

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:41.804
- I have like a metropolis.

00:01:41.804 --> 00:01:42.690
- [Alison] Yeah, yeah.

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:43.523
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:43.523 --> 00:01:44.356
- Oh my God.

00:01:44.356 --> 00:01:45.300
- I'm like that crazy lady.
- I love it.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.285
- I have all the Charles Dickens,

00:01:46.285 --> 00:01:47.607
like, I have all of it, yep.

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.680
- Oh, oh, my, this movie is for you.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:50.513
Okay, so then-
- Okay.

00:01:50.513 --> 00:01:53.674
- But because the little
girl, my character's daughter,

00:01:53.674 --> 00:01:56.100
makes a wish when she's putting together

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:56.933
the Christmas village-

00:01:56.933 --> 00:01:57.766
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:57.766 --> 00:01:59.430
- It maybe has a little magic-
- Ohh.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.263
- Where it's helping,

00:02:00.263 --> 00:02:01.723
like she plays with the
figurines, and they-

00:02:01.723 --> 00:02:02.970
- I love when magic is involved.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:03.803
- I do too.

00:02:03.803 --> 00:02:04.636
- Yes.

00:02:04.636 --> 00:02:05.920
- Especially Christmas magic.
- Life needs it.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:08.370
- Yeah, yes, so then we
created these characters

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:09.203
for my character, Summer.

00:02:09.203 --> 00:02:11.165
She's, you know, she's
got her life together.

00:02:11.165 --> 00:02:12.165
She's a single mom.

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:14.145
She's got, you know,
all her ducks in a row.

00:02:14.145 --> 00:02:16.296
And so she needed a little magic

00:02:16.296 --> 00:02:18.696
to like get her off her game,

00:02:18.696 --> 00:02:21.325
to meet up with this guy she
would never have normally met.

00:02:21.325 --> 00:02:22.176
- Yeah.
- You know?

00:02:22.176 --> 00:02:24.810
So the Christmas village
sort of brings them together.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:25.643
- And it's Luke, right?

00:02:25.643 --> 00:02:26.755
I just had Luke on here.
- Yes, yes, he told me

00:02:26.755 --> 00:02:28.497
that he was just here.
- I love him.

00:02:28.497 --> 00:02:29.926
He's so nice.

00:02:29.926 --> 00:02:31.380
- Such a nice guy.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.490
We had so much fun.
- Yeah, and funny.

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:33.720
- And he's super funny.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:34.553
- Like his wit, I was like,

00:02:34.553 --> 00:02:35.490
"Well that was under the radar."

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:36.323
I was like, yeah.

00:02:36.323 --> 00:02:37.470
- He's really, really funny.

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:38.606
But he's also super romantic.

00:02:38.606 --> 00:02:39.915
He's so great in this movie.

00:02:39.915 --> 00:02:41.190
He's, it was really fun.

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:42.120
- He loves country music.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:42.953
Of course he's romantic.

00:02:42.953 --> 00:02:43.786
- [Alison] Yeah.

00:02:43.786 --> 00:02:44.619
(audience laughs)

00:02:44.619 --> 00:02:45.452
He was like, "I love
me some Garth Brooks."

00:02:45.452 --> 00:02:46.285
I'm like, "I'm sorry, what?"

00:02:46.285 --> 00:02:47.574
I was like, "That's awesome."

00:02:47.574 --> 00:02:48.407
(audience clapping)

00:02:48.407 --> 00:02:49.380
Well, you produced this movie

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:50.390
and you have more in store
with Hallmark, right?

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:52.185
- Yes.
- Did you do like a deal?

00:02:52.185 --> 00:02:53.044
I heard a deal, yeah.
- I do have a deal

00:02:53.044 --> 00:02:54.330
with Hallmark.

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:56.340
They are so wonderful to work with,

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:57.173
super supportive of-

00:02:57.173 --> 00:02:59.700
- Everybody that works with
them says they love their lives.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:01.642
- Yeah, yeah, because they're
just really supportive

00:03:01.642 --> 00:03:04.964
of like telling these female
stories, you know, helping.

00:03:04.964 --> 00:03:08.516
I like to bring in a lot of
female directors also, so-

00:03:08.516 --> 00:03:09.484
- And they make you feel good.

00:03:09.484 --> 00:03:10.735
- And they do, yes.

00:03:10.735 --> 00:03:11.844
They're really empowering

00:03:11.844 --> 00:03:13.185
and I love working with them, so yes,

00:03:13.185 --> 00:03:17.280
I have other projects I'm
working on for next year,

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.244
which I'm really excited to come back

00:03:18.244 --> 00:03:19.560
and tell you all about.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:20.393
- Yeah, that's cool,
(audience clapping)

00:03:20.393 --> 00:03:22.695
because now you get to
like find stories too-

00:03:22.695 --> 00:03:24.000
- Yes.
- That maybe you like,

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.110
and you get to produce those, that's cool.

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:27.870
- Yeah, no, I love reading
stories, reading books,

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:31.036
finding IP that I wanna
turn into movies, right?

00:03:31.036 --> 00:03:32.130
- Yeah, absolutely.
- You know, it's like,

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:34.135
and I feel like I'm the Hallmark audience.

00:03:34.135 --> 00:03:36.876
I'm that person who wants to
watch these romantic comedies.

00:03:36.876 --> 00:03:39.210
They're not making them in
feature films anymore, so,

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:40.260
or on the movie screen.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:41.093
- They really aren't.
- So like, yeah,

00:03:41.093 --> 00:03:42.375
come watch Hallmark on a Friday night.

00:03:42.375 --> 00:03:43.380
- Yeah.

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:44.213
- [Alison] We're in.

00:03:44.213 --> 00:03:45.046
- We love them.

00:03:45.046 --> 00:03:45.879
- I love rom-coms.
- I know.

00:03:45.879 --> 00:03:49.335
- So this year you celebrated
the, is it your 30th year?

00:03:49.335 --> 00:03:50.250
- Yes, oh-

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:51.084
- [Kelly] On "Days of Our Lives?"

00:03:51.084 --> 00:03:53.263
(audience cheers)
- I don't do the math a lot.

00:03:54.383 --> 00:03:57.000
- That's, like, you
pretty much find people

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.200
you like to work with, and you say-

00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:59.370
- Yeah, yeah, I'm loyal.

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:00.455
I stick around.
- That's really good though,

00:04:00.455 --> 00:04:02.744
that it means also that
it's a great environment.

00:04:02.744 --> 00:04:03.780
So that's awesome.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:04.613
What do you think

00:04:04.613 --> 00:04:05.446
about 30 years?
- I feel like I grew up

00:04:05.446 --> 00:04:07.830
playing this character,
playing Sami Brady.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:09.720
I started when I was 16 years old,

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:10.567
and I was-
- Oh my gosh.

00:04:10.567 --> 00:04:13.890
- Dopey kid and I just loved it.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:15.000
I love my job.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:15.865
I love working there.

00:04:15.865 --> 00:04:19.396
The crew, like how all
watched me grow up and-

00:04:19.396 --> 00:04:20.229
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:20.229 --> 00:04:21.990
- Get married and have my own kids.

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:23.970
And then now I get to go
back every once in a while

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:26.655
and visit, and you do get that sense

00:04:26.655 --> 00:04:28.860
of just reuniting with everyone again.

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:29.810
- Yeah, that's wonderful.

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:32.490
Well, "A Magical Christmas
Village" premieres tonight

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:34.173
on Hallmark Channel at eight.

